          "worked": "The squared terms are $(4x^2)^2$ and $3^2$. Check: $2\\times4x^2\\times3=24x^2$.\n$$16x^4+24x^2+9=(4x^2+3)^2$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$36-12x+x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(6-x)^2$",
          "worked": "The squared terms are $6^2$ and $x^2$. Check: $2\\times6\\times x=12x$. The middle term is negative.\n$$36-12x+x^2=(6-x)^2$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q6-d",
